# Game object architecture

Everything in the world is a game object. Keep entity state on objects, not in loose functions or renderer globals.

## Components

Describe an object as a container of components. Put data and behavior on components instead of growing one subclass.

```javascript
const player = {
  id: 'player',
  components: { transform, health, input },
}
```

## Tick

Update object state in one tick loop. Do not change simulation state from render callbacks or one-off timers.

```javascript
function tick(dt) {
  for (const object of scene.objects) object.update(dt)
}
```

## Events

Objects interact by emitting and listening to events. Do not reach into another object and call its internals.

```javascript
object.emit('hit', { source, amount })
```

## Scene

The scene owns add, remove, and lookup. Query the scene instead of keeping a second object list.
